    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d73-a1">

                <pb facs="0191" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg103"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January 30,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Supplementing my note of September 30 to Mr. David E. Thompson, I now have the
                    honor to inform you that, according to the declaration of my colleague of the
                    navy, the Brazilian firm of Rosa, Carvalho &amp; Co., of Pelotas, has already
                    ordered the flag used on its ships to be substituted, complying thus with the
                    request contained in the note from your legation of May 25 last.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio Branco.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
